<title>POLAND: Polish NBP sells marks at PLN 1.9395-dealers.</title>
<headline>Polish NBP sells marks at PLN 1.9395-dealers.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland (NBP) sold marks on the interbank market at 1.9395 zlotys, dealers said.</p>
<p>The intervention, described as &quot;medium,&quot;came at 1138 GMT when the zloty was about 3.5 percent from Friday's dollar/mark parity rate , or the centre of the daily 14-percent trading band.</p>
<p>Earlier, the NBP also sold dollars at 3.4911 and 3.4880 zlotys. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
